Vendored modules -- attribution
==============================

The contents of this directory are verbatim copies of modules originally
written for the (private) Atlas research codebase, redistributed here so
that the public reproduction package is self-contained.

Vendored contents:
  aoa_v3/                   -- the full pipeline package (embed, dmap, gw,
                               barycenter, aoa, sensitivity, predict, data,
                               viz, and supporting loaders)
  config.py                 -- pipeline configuration dataclasses
  embed.py                  -- Takens delay embedding + AMI/FNN selection
  diffuse.py                -- per-series diffusion maps (dense + Nystrom)
  landscape.py              -- domain / universal landscape objects
  transport.py              -- transport-plan DMAP coordinates
  synthetic_gate.py         -- synthetic validation gate (12-family zoo)
  eps008_complete_layer1.py -- layer 1-3 results at eps = 0.008

Copyright (c) Maximilian Topel; redistributed under the MIT license of the
parent this repository:  package (see ../LICENSE).

These modules depend only on packages listed in this repository: requirements.txt.
aoa_repro.config.use_vendor() adds this directory to sys.path so the bare
`from config import ...` / `from embed import ...` statements inside the
vendored modules resolve; aoa_repro/_vendor/ keeps the original minimal trio
(embed, diffuse, config) for back-compat.

If the Atlas modules are subsequently published as a standalone package,
this directory should be replaced with an ordinary dependency declaration
in requirements.txt and the local files removed.
